    "forensics": "The losing cluster stems from two primary failure modes: tight stop-loss whipsaws (0.45% min_sl_pct) during the 10:25\u201310:40 IST post-opening range mean-reversion window (TATASTEEL, INFY, NTPC), and late-session (14:25\u201314:30 IST) momentum exhaustion (COALINDIA, ICICIBANK). In the latter, trades lacked the time and volume expansion to reach the 1.2% target before EOD square-off, allowing statutory brokerage and exchange fees (\u20b936.66 total vs \u20b9-32.02 net P&L) to turn flat/marginally positive gross moves into net losses.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE large-cap cash equities, 10:30 IST breakout sweeps with moderate volume (2.0x) frequently revert within a 0.50%-0.65% noise band, requiring wider structural stops, higher volume conviction, and faster breakeven ratchets to neutralize transaction fee drag on small-capital allocations.",
